# Testing Standards

## Fixtures (defined in `tests/conftest.py`)
- `engine` / `session` — in-memory SQLite, never the real DB
- `sample_prospect` — a Company with type="prospect"
- `sample_competitor` — a Company with type="competitor"
- `sample_signals` — 5 signals attached to sample_prospect

## Patterns
- One test file per source module (`test_models.py`, `test_scoring.py`, etc.)
- Group in classes: `class TestRecencyDecay`, `class TestFundingClassification`
- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` for testing regex/keyword classifiers against many inputs
- `pytest.approx()` for float comparisons (never `==` on floats)
- To test a method without full collector init:

```python
collector = FundingCollector.__new__(FundingCollector)
result = collector._classify_funding("company raised $50m")
```

## Scope
- Test: scoring math, regex classifiers, keyword matchers, model relationships, AI fallbacks, edge cases
- Skip: Streamlit rendering, external HTTP calls, SQLAlchemy/SQLite internals
